<Project Sdk="AsmFoundation.Sdk">
  <!--
    The GrpcAsm engine: HTTP/2 (h2n), HPACK (hpack), the gRPC call layer (grpc), the epoll
    worker (worker), the server's lifecycle (server: ga_server_run), the per-worker allocator
    (pool), structured logging (log) and helpers (util), moved out of KvAsm
    (AsmFoundation/KvAsm server/src at 60d7e81).

    Milestone B: step 1 split the files, step 2 renamed the engine's exports to ga_*, step 3
    made the application hooks the only way the engine calls out (the ga_app_* symbols declared
    and documented in include/grpcasm_hooks.inc, which an application such as samples/KvServer
    defines and the linker binds), step 4 moved the generic half of KvAsm's grpc.asm in here
    (body buffering, validation, the health service, stream release), step 5a replaced
    KvAsm's hard-coded routes with the application's route table (ga_app_routes,
    include/grpcasm_routes.inc), and step 5b moved the server's lifecycle in here
    (ga_server_run), with samples/Greeter as the generic test service (docs/ROADMAP.md).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>StaticLibrary</OutputType>
    <!-- libc: the engine calls glibc (pthread_create, the allocator) through the PLT, so only a
         libc program can link it, and NuGet refuses it to a freestanding project (NU1201)
         instead of a link failing later. -->
    <TargetFramework>libc</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>grpcasm</AssemblyName>
    <!-- PackageId defaults to AssemblyName, as in .NET, and GrpcAsm.Native's is grpcasm too
         (libgrpcasm.so): two projects of one restore graph with the same name are
         "Ambiguous project name 'grpcasm'" to NuGet. The package is GrpcAsm (milestone E). -->
    <PackageId>GrpcAsm</PackageId>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
